## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | **3** (across 10 tests) |
| **Medium** | **2** |

**Diagnosis: This is a textbook coverage-touching test suite.** All 10 tests exercise production methods, achieving high line coverage, but **7 out of 10 tests have zero meaningful assertions**. The remaining 3 use only `Assert.IsNotNull` — the weakest possible check. Every production method could return garbage, mutate the wrong data, or silently corrupt state and all 10 tests would still pass green.

---

### 🔴 Critical Findings

#### 1. No Assertions (7 tests)

These tests call production code and discard results with no verification at all:

| Test Method | Line | What It Misses |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` | 17–21 | Never verifies the product was actually saved |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | 33–36 | Never checks the price actually changed |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | 39–42 | Never confirms the product was deleted |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 64–66 | Captures count in nothing — no `var`, no assert |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 69–74 | Never verifies any price was discounted |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 85–88 | Never checks any product was imported |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 64–66 | Doesn't even add products first — asserts nothing about 0 |

**Fix for `AddProduct_Works` (representative pattern for all 7):**
```csharp
// BEFORE — coverage-touching, no assertion
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_Works()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
}

// AFTER — verifies observable behavior
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_ProductIsRetrievable()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}
```

**Fix for `UpdatePrice_Works`:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
}
```

**Fix for `RemoveProduct_Works`:**
